  "name": "cloud-armor-crs-rule-upgrader",
  "description": "Upgrades Google Cloud Armor security policies from OWASP CRS 3.0 and 3.3 to OWASP CRS 4.22. Preserves signature opt-in and opt-out lists, translates evaluatePreconfiguredExpr to native evaluatePreconfiguredWaf dictionary parameters, remaps signature IDs to v042200, drops retired signature IDs, and updates structured preconfiguredWafConfig fine-tuning exclusions. Evaluates operational risk (High Breaking Change, Medium Attention Required, Low Clean Upgrade) including Method Enforcement breaking changes (PUT/PATCH/DELETE blocking) and sensitivity coverage expansions. Supports both in-place rule upgrades and smooth preview mode deployments with priority spacing and a 200-rule quota guardrail. Use when a user or agent needs to audit, upgrade, or transition Cloud Armor WAF rules to CRS 4.22. Don't use for non-WAF Cloud Armor rules (IP rate-limiting, geo-blocking, reCAPTCHA) or AWS/Azure WAF migrations.",
